 se veía desde los sesenta. Nueva York: Adrenalin O.D., el straight-edge de Youth Of Today y Gorilla Biscuits, el crossover punk-metal (Cro-Mags, Prong, Danzig). Washington lanza a Pussy Galore (la irrelevancia hecha relevante), Unrest y Fugazi de Ian MacKaye, que abstrae el hardcore en una forma teatral de compromiso ético y estético (Repeater, Steady Diet Of Nothing, Red Medicine), y Royal Trux (Twin Infinitives, «un Trout Mask Replica para la generación grunge»). El punk-pop de Mr T Experience, Dwarves, Henry Rollins, L7 (pioneras del «foxcore»), Lemonheads, Screeching Weasel, Goo Goo Dolls, Fastbacks, Shonen Knife; el «rogue folk» de los Pogues, Membranes y Chumbawamba.","color":"#fb7185","family":"Punk, new wave, hardcore y noise","link":"https://volteret4.github.io/scaruffi/#punk-crossover"}],"book_tracks":[{"id":143872780593219,"artist":"Prong","artist_id":209524554197097,"title":"Force Fed","year":1988,"ess":0,"yt":"QtzrnGvkAU0","kind":"a","book":{"id":8,"title":"A History of Rock Music 1951-2000","author":"Piero Scaruffi","url":"https://volteret4.github.io/scaruffi/"},"scene":"Cruces del punk: de Fugazi al punk-pop","scene_id":203478263290546,"scene_link":"https://volteret4.github.io/scaruffi/#punk-crossover","chapters":["Sección 5.23"],"pages":[[1,213,null]]}],"mentions":[{"book":"A History of Rock Music 1951-2000","author":"Piero Scaruffi","page":213,"text":"…In New York, the genre's artistic peak came later into the decade with Cro-Mags (1), particularly their second album Best Wishes (1989), and Prong (1), who boasted the most brutal \"grooves\" also on their second album, Force Fed (1988). Danzig (1) continued his messianic saga under his own name,…"}],"podcast":[],"awards":[],"concerts":[],"xref":[{"kind":"xref","title":"Project History (1995-2004)","body":"This project was created in 1995 and involved Trent Reznor, Atticus Ross, and a variety of friends, continuing off and on for nine years. Despite the collaboration, nothing was ever officially released. \"I already mentioned the tapeworm project, which was created in 1995 and included a lot of different friends. They were continued off and on for nine years, but nothing was ever released.\"","year":1995,"extra":{"from":"Tapeworm","from_id":3612399909254,"type":"curiosity"},"srcs":[{"source":"The Ongoing History of New Music","episode":"9 Nine In Nails Tales","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=DKdF8NgF5Bw"}]},{"kind":"xref","title":"Broadway Musical Character","body":"John Bechtel is the touring keyboard player for Ministry and has also played with Fear Factory, Killing Joke, and Prong. He is a character in both the graphic novel *Funhouse* and its subsequent Broadway musical adaptation, which were created by his sister, Alice Bechtel. \"John is actually a character in both, but Alice is best known for creating the Bechtel Test, which is the test that measures the representation of women in fiction.\"","year":null,"extra":{"from":"John Bechtel","from_id":212473741741682,"type":"curiosity"},"srcs":[{"source":"The Ongoing History of New Music","episode":"60 Mind Blowing Facts in 60 Minutes: The 5th Edition","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=72Lei7uug8c"}]}],"charts":[{"id":39767070562525,"type":"album","name":"Primitive Origins","list_id":260496355374042,"list":"RYM Top — Rock — Crossover Thrash","src":"musthear","rank":97,"year":1987,"note":null,"yt":"RAOd72GJ9qE","scaruffi":null},{"id":143872780593219,"type":"album","name":"Force Fed","list_id":260496355374042,"list":"RYM Top — Rock — Crossover Thrash","src":"musthear","rank":92,"year":1988,"note":null,"yt":"QtzrnGvkAU0","scaruffi":7.0},{"id":143872780593219,"type":"album","name":"Force Fed","list_id":52032266791182,"list":"Scaruffi 1980s","src":"musthear","rank":652,"year":1988,"note":null,"yt":"QtzrnGvkAU0","scaruffi":7.0},{"id":226677483978331,"type":"album","name":"Beg To Differ","list_id":60939677007180,"list":"RYM Top — Rock — Groove Metal","src":"musthear","rank":35,"year":1990,"note":null,"yt"